+
+@opcode{capsminpartialword, minimum wordlimit}
+Use individual capital-letter indicators for a capitals run shorter than
+@var{minimum} when it ends inside a mixed-case word containing at most
+@var{wordlimit} cased letters. Count the complete surrounding word, not
+only the capitals run and its following lowercase letters. Words with
+non-cased symbols between their cased letters are excluded. The option
+requires @var{minimum} from 2 to 16 and @var{wordlimit} from @var{minimum}
+to 32. It is disabled unless declared. Complete capitals words, longer
+mixed-case words, and other emphasis classes retain their usual indicators.
+For example, @code{capsminpartialword 3 3} uses individual indicators in
+@code{ABc}, but keeps the existing word indicators in @code{ABC},
+@code{ABcd}, @code{xABc}, and @code{aBC}.
 
 @opcode{capsphrasevar, variable}
 Expose the sentence-wide capitals-passage analysis to forward context
